1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,480
 Here's how I make my iPhone footage look like my $5,000 Sony camera.

2
00:00:03,720 --> 00:00:06,880
 This is day 25 of helping you get better at content creation.

3
00:00:07,060 --> 00:00:09,080
 Now let's turn your iPhone into a cinema camera.

4
00:00:09,260 --> 00:00:11,180
 First, download the Blackmagic Camera app.

5
00:00:11,260 --> 00:00:13,900
 Go to Settings and under Color Space, select Apple Log.

6
00:00:13,980 --> 00:00:15,060
 Use these camera settings.

7
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:16,720
 Set the lens to 24mm.

8
00:00:16,880 --> 00:00:18,380
 The frame rate to 25fps.

9
00:00:18,660 --> 00:00:20,120
 The shutter speed to 1 over 50.

10
00:00:20,220 --> 00:00:21,300
 The ISO to 100.

11
00:00:21,540 --> 00:00:22,480
 Record your footage.

12
00:00:22,680 --> 00:00:24,540
 Import your footage into DaVinci Resolve.

13
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:28,720
 Apply my Apple Log LUT, which will instantly transform your flat footage into something cinematic.

14
00:00:28,720 --> 00:00:31,940
 And just like that, you've got professional camera quality just from your iPhone.

15
00:00:32,060 --> 00:00:36,000
 If you want my Apple Log LUT, then comment LUT down below and I'll send it to you for free.

